{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And Joseph died, being one hundred and ten years old.</b> Joseph buried his father Jacob, and received his reward through one who was greater than both of them — this is Moses our master, peace be upon him — who occupied himself with his bones, as it is said, ״ויקח משה את עצמות יוסף עמו.״ And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: What did Moses do? He took a tablet and cast it into the Nile, and wrote upon it עלה שור עלה שור, and he said to him: Joseph, Joseph! Your brothers are being redeemed, and the Shekhinah is held back on your account, and the clouds of glory are held back on your account. If it is your will to be revealed and to come up — come up; and if not, we are released from your oath. For the Egyptians wanted to hide him so that his brothers would never find him, and they made for him a metal coffin and placed it in the Nile — and this is what is written, <b>and he was placed in a coffin in Egypt.</b> Likewise Moses our master, peace be upon him, who occupied himself with Joseph, received his reward through one greater than himself — this is the Holy One, blessed be He — as it is said (Deuteronomy 34): ״ויקבור אותו בגי״. From here we learn that whoever exerts himself in commandments to perform them has great and abundant reward: if in his lifetime, his good deed yields its fruit from afar; and if after his death, his reward is with him, inscribed in a book that is never erased. Therefore a person is obligated to perform the commandments with alacrity, not with laziness, not for his own honor but for the honor of Heaven — to serve the service of HaShem, may He be exalted, to keep His charge, to delight in His Torah, to strengthen oneself in His hope, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 131): ״יחל ישראל אל ה' מעתה ועד עולם״, and it is written (Psalms 31): ״חזקו ויאמץ לבבכם כל המיחלים לה'״. Blessed is the man who trusts in HaShem, and HaShem is his trust. Trust in HaShem forever, for in HaShem is the Rock of worlds. <br><small>End of the book of Genesis.</small>"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:10.070332261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}